  "name": "Repurpose YouTube videos into weekly LinkedIn and Bluesky posts with Gemini and PostWire",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "1badfa2b-f0d7-43de-a1d7-a45f444c6f18",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -640,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 721,
        "content": "## Turn one YouTube video into a week of posts\nPaste a YouTube link in a form. Gemini watches the video and pulls out its key points, and PostWire writes one post per day for LinkedIn and Bluesky and schedules the whole week.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Paste a YouTube link** takes the link, an optional angle and how many days to fill. **Is a YouTube link** stops anything else.\n2. **Watch the video with Gemini** sends the link to Gemini, which watches the video itself (no transcript service) and returns a summary and one takeaway per day. **Build the brief** reads the answer.\n3. **Plan a week of posts** (PostWire) writes a different post for each day and network in your voice and queues one per day.\n4. **Log the scheduled posts** adds a row per day and **Email me the plan** sends you the week.\n5. If Gemini cannot read the video or PostWire refuses, **Log the failure** and **Email me the fix** tell you what to fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Add a Google Gemini credential to **Watch the video with Gemini** (the free tier works with public videos).\n3. Create a sheet with the columns date, video, title, goes_out, status, post, link and note, and pick it in both Sheets nodes.\n4. Connect Gmail and fill in **Your voice and email**.\n\n### Customize\nChange the posting hour or the voice in **Your voice and email**, or add facebook or mastodon to the PostWire node (the free PostWire plan posts to 2 networks per post)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
